From: helmfile-enhancement-plan
Subject: [PATCH] PR-T-02 — Fix dte/Makefile:test glob to actually run all 70 tests

Closes G2 (test glob misses distributed-worker/).
Branch: chore/dte-makefile-fix-test-glob

The current targets reference ./cmd/... which does not exist; the result
is that go test silently runs only the 6 tests under pkg/logger and ignores
the 64 tests under distributed-worker/. This patch:
  - replaces the bogus glob with ./...
  - adds -race
  - generates a coverage profile
  - removes the `|| echo` that swallows failures.

---
 atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/dte/Makefile | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/dte/Makefile b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/dte/Makefile
--- a/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/dte/Makefile
+++ b/atlassian_packages/gcp_kitt/helmfile/dte/Makefile
@@ -41,12 +41,12 @@ build: ## Build the binary
 .PHONY: test
 test: ## Run tests
 	@echo "Running tests..."
-	go test ./pkg/... ./cmd/... || echo "No tests found or tests failed"
+	go test -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
+	@go tool cover -func=coverage.out | tail -1

 .PHONY: test-verbose
 test-verbose: ## Run tests with verbose output
 	@echo "Running tests with verbose output..."
-	go test -v ./pkg/... ./cmd/...
+	go test -race -v ./...
